#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186075046 :tutorial/content "To divide a whole number by a unit fraction, we can multiply the whole number by the fraction's denominator.\n\nSo, to divide $2 \\div \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5},$ we multiply the $2$ by ${\\color{blue}5}\\!:$\n\n$$\n2 \\div \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5} = 2 \\times {\\color{blue}5} = 10\n$$\n\nAnd that's the answer! Notice that this method does the same job as the fraction model method we used before:\n\n![](images/5f/5f2eb6ab39ea67466d7a42a8809b8a039a84f9a20a13cca3659d81f669a772a5.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "058743c7-e03e-521c-92ce-c1a5fd00663f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8572 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
